  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "Can I read fuel level remotely on a Audi A3?",
      "a": "Yes, with a DIMO device. Query the powertrainFuelSystemRelativeLevel or powertrainFuelSystemAbsoluteLevel signal through the Telemetry API. For refuel events, the segments query accepts the refuel detection mechanism, which looks for a significant rise in fuel level."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I track a Audi A3 with no connected services?",
      "a": "Use a DIMO device. Once the vehicle is connected and shared with your Developer License, exchange your Developer JWT for a Vehicle JWT through the Token Exchange API. Then read signals and trip segments from the Telemetry API."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I detect idling on a Audi A3?",
      "a": "Idling is listed as an event for this vehicle on a DIMO device. Call the segments query in the Telemetry API with the idling detection mechanism, which finds periods where engine RPM stays in the idle range. You can adjust the idle threshold with maxIdleRpm in the config."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I verify Audi A3 mileage?",
      "a": "Use a DIMO device to supply the odometer signal. Then request an odometer statement attestation with a POST to /v2/attestation/odometer-statement/:tokenId on the Attestation API. Retrieve the rawVC through the Telemetry API."
    }
  ],
  "intro": "DIMO gives developers API access to vehicle-state data: diagnostics, fault codes, battery and fuel health, odometer, and maintenance signals. For the Audi A3, data comes from a DIMO device, covering model years 2010 and newer. This coverage has been tested rather than assumed, and you query it through the Telemetry API with a Vehicle JWT. DIMO adds vehicle-state depth on top of GPS tracking; it doesn't replace it."
